{"step_index":1326,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:55:47Z","input_tokens":2088,"cache_read_tokens":303310,"output_tokens":6334,"thinking":"The analysis of `verify_hardened.cjs` indicates a potential issue within the `getEl` function (lines 53-92). Suspect that `AbortController` must be passed in `ctx` on line 105. Additionally, the code either needs to use `initClassesFromHtml` for `classList`, or it needs to check if `dashRows[0].children[0]` is initialized correctly.\n\n\nThe initial focus was on verifying `verify_hardened.cjs`, but analysis shifted to `scratch\\obf_tool\\verify_dashboard.cjs` to create tests for Patch 1.0.25. The code appears to correctly initialize elements without the need for `classList` during element creation or appending.\n\nTesting for the landing screen without `?quiz=` is underway. This test will ensure specific elements are visible or hidden according to the requirements, and that the `:runQuery` `POST` projection renders the correct quiz elements with expected buttons.\n\n\nVerifying the rename functionality, starting with a valid rename of a dashboard row and observing the expected label and database update. Tests also cover empty rename validations and sanitized handling of reserved Windows filenames.\n\nFurther tests confirm the \"Add more Quiz\" button correctly creates a new quiz row in the dashboard, and that the new quiz persists across dashboard reloads. Verifying quiz loading transitions to the quiz editor and the submissions tab correctly.\n\n\nTesting the download functionality, I am validating that the file name matches the quiz title, including handling special characters in the filename. Successfully tested downloading different quiz titles. Further tests focused on verifying the correct `quizId` is extracted when the downloaded HTML is opened offline. The system now confirms the correct quiz ID is used for GET requests and submissions, while maintaining independent locks for each quiz.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"const fs = require('fs');\nconst vm = require('vm');\n\nconst idxHtml = fs.readFileSync('C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\Desktop\\\\Exploit\\\\index.html', 'utf8');\nconst tchHtml = fs.readFileSync('C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\Desktop\\\\Exploit\\\\teacher.html', 'utf8');\n\nfunction extractRuntime(html) {\n  const c = /<script\\s+id=[\"']local-runtime-cipher[\"'][^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/script>/i.exec(html)[1];\n  const v = /<script\\s+id=[\"']local-db-vault[\"'][^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/script>/i.exec(html);\n  const s = html.lastIndexOf('<script>');\n  const e = html.lastIndexOf('</script>');\n  return { cipher: c, vault: v ? v[1] : '', boot: html.slice(s + 8, e), html };\n}\n\nconst idxRt = extractRuntime(idxHtml);\nconst tchRt = extractRuntime(tchHtml);\n\nfunction makeEnv(rt, { customFetch, initialStorage, searchStr = '', vaultOverride } = {}) {\n  const els = {};\n  const lsStore = new Map(Object.entries(initialStorage || {}));\n  const createdDownloads = [];\n  let lastCreatedBlob = null;\n\n  const initClassesFromHtml = id => {\n    const re = new RegExp(`id=[\"']${id}[\"'][^>]*class=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']`, 'i');\n    const m = re.exec(rt.html);\n    return m ? m[1].split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean) : [];\n  };\n\n  const mkClassList = init => {\n    const set = new Set(init);\n    return {\n      add(c) { set.add(c); },\n      remove(c) { set.delete(c); },\n      contains(c) { return set.has(c); },\n      toggle(c, force) {\n        if (force === true) { set.add(c); return true; }\n        if (force === false) { set.delete(c); return false; }\n        if (set.has(c)) { set.delete(c); return false; }\n        set.add(c); return true;\n      }\n    };\n  };\n\n  const mkNode = (tag, initClasses = []) => {\n    const node = {\n      tagName: tag.toUpperCase(),\n      className: initClasses.join(' '),\n      style: {},\n      disabled: false,\n      value: '',\n      textContent: '',\n      innerHTML: '',\n      download: '',\n      href: '',\n      classList: mkClassList(initClasses),\n      children: [],\n      onclick: null,\n      focus() {},\n      scrollIntoView() {},\n      append(...a) { this.children.push(...a); },\n      appendChild(a) { this.children.push(a); },\n      querySelectorAll(sel) { return sel === '.q-card' ? this.children : []; },\n      querySelector(sel) {\n        const find = cls => {\n          for (const lb of this.children) for (const ch of (lb.children || [])) if (String(ch.className || '').includes(cls)) return ch;\n          return { value: '' };\n        };\n        const map = { '.q-text': 'q-text', '.q-corr': 'q-corr', '.q-w1': 'q-w1', '.q-w2': 'q-w2', '.q-w3': 'q-w3', '.q-exp': 'q-exp' };\n        return map[sel] ? find(map[sel]) : { value: '', textContent: '' };\n      },\n      click() {\n        if (this.tagName === 'A' && this.download) {\n          createdDownloads.push({ download: this.download, href: this.href });\n        }\n      },\n      remove() {},\n      parentNode: { removeChild() {} }\n    };\n    return node;\n  };\n\n  const getEl = id => {\n    if (id === 'local-runtime-cipher') return { textContent: rt.cipher };\n    if (id === 'local-db-vault') return { textContent: vaultOverride !== undefined ? vaultOverride : rt.vault };\n    if (!els[id]) {\n      els[id] = mkNode('div', initClassesFromHtml(id));\n      els[id].id = id;\n      if (id === 'go') els[id].disabled = true;\n      if (id === 'wc') els[id].textContent = '0';\n    }\n    return els[id];\n  };\n\n  [\n    'start','title','desc','nm','sc','err','go','lock','lk1','lk2','lkdl','exam','prog','sw','tm','pbar','tb','q','opts','nx','res','rn','rs','rd','res-actions','dl','cp','res-note','fbs','wm','warn','wp','wc','wbtn',\n    'main-nav','tab-btn-dash','tab-btn-editor','tab-btn-sub','view-dash','dash-list','dash-msg','add-quiz-btn','active-quiz-badge','rename-modal','rename-input','rename-save-btn','rename-cancel-btn','view-editor','view-sub','qtitle',